@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il05-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il05-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-k`
IMPORT `nii-s348-maximum-minimum`
IMPORT `nii-s342-liability-and-deduction`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for row IL-05, by the independent test author (fid-il-05).
-- Every expected value below was decided in DECIDED-ANSWERS.md from the Hebrew source, the two
-- deposited amending Laws and the National Insurance Institute's pages, BEFORE any .l4 file or
-- NOTES.md of this encoding was opened. Each assertion is tagged with its scenario id there.
-- An assertion that fails is a finding; none has been edited to match the encoding.
-- Assertions marked SUPPLEMENTARY were added after seeing the interface, to separate a root cause;
-- their expected values follow the decided rule, at a different input.
--
-- Inputs are this author's, not the encoding's (DECIDED-ANSWERS.md section 1): basic amount 10,382;
-- average wage for contributions 13,769 (s 1 as modified by s 2(b)); reduced bracket 7,703; monthly
-- minimum wage 6,247.67 (January 2026) and 6,443.85 (from April 2026).

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Fixtures`

`fid 2026 figures` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2026
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS 10382
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS 13769
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS EMPTY

-- F12: an invented compensation update on 1 April 2026 to 14,000.
`fid 2026 figures with an April update` MEANS
    `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS 2026
        `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS 10382
        `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS 13769
        `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS
            LIST (`An update of the average wage within the tax year` WITH `the month of the update` IS 4, `the average wage as updated` IS 14000)

`fid 2026 minimum wages` MEANS
    `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter` WITH
        `in January` IS 6247.67
        `in April`   IS 6443.85
        `in July`    IS 6443.85
        `in October` IS 6443.85

`fid Q1` MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 January`
`fid Q2` MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 April`
`fid Q3` MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 July`
`fid Q4` MEANS `a quarter of the tax year` `the quarter beginning on 1 October`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A period under Schedule K`
`fid month` n MEANS `a month of the tax year` n

`fid year` MEANS `the whole tax year`

-- The s 348 case, every field.
GIVEN y       IS A NUMBER
      p       IS A `A period under Schedule K`
      col     IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      work    IS A NUMBER
      nonwork IS A NUMBER
      w       IS A MAYBE `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
      unemp   IS A BOOLEAN
      vol     IS A BOOLEAN
      yeshiva IS A BOOLEAN
      ncs     IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid case` y p col work nonwork w unemp vol yeshiva ncs MEANS
    `An insured person's period under section 348` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS y
        `period`                                                              IS p
        `column`                                                              IS col
        `income from work in the period`                                      IS work
        `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`    IS nonwork
        `the minimum wage applicable to the employee`                         IS w
        `received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G`      IS unemp
        `a volunteer in national service or in community volunteering`        IS vol
        `a student in a Torah institution or in a yeshiva`                    IS yeshiva
        `serving in civil service as defined in section 6(a) of the Deferral of Service for Yeshiva Students Law` IS FALSE
        `the day the person began national-civic service, if serving in it`   IS ncs
        `section 350(c) disapplies section 348(b) to the person`              IS FALSE
        `an order under section 348(c) has changed a minimum amount for the period` IS FALSE

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, p IS A `A period under Schedule K`, work IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid employee case` y p work MEANS
    `fid case` y p `an employee` work 0 (JUST `fid 2026 minimum wages`) FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, p IS A `A period under Schedule K`, work IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid self-employed case` y p work MEANS
    `fid case` y p `a self-employed person` work 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, p IS A `A period under Schedule K`, work IS A NUMBER, nonwork IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid neither case` y p work nonwork MEANS
    `fid case` y p `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` work nonwork NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

-- A yeshiva student who is neither employee nor self-employed. NOTE: the encoding has no field for a
-- non-employee's income other than "income from work" and "income not from work"; the quarterly
-- yeshiva cases below put their income in "income from work" because (a1) on a quarter refuses.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, p IS A `A period under Schedule K`, work IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid yeshiva case` y p work MEANS
    `fid case` y p `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` work 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, p IS A `A period under Schedule K`, began IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid national-civic service case` y p began MEANS
    `fid case` y p `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` 0 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST began)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, p IS A `A period under Schedule K`, nonwork IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`fid unemployment case` y p nonwork MEANS
    `fid case` y p `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` 0 nonwork NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

-- Schedule J column D, from its ROWS (source lines 4720-4729, temporary text 2025-2026), applied to a
-- wage split at the bracket 7,703: (part above, part not above) per branch. The three branches column D
-- prints "–" for carry 0. The caller (this author) applies any cap: the encoding does not.
GIVEN `the wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
`fid column D amounts on a wage of` `the wage` MEANS
    LIST (`A branch's column D amount` OF `maternity`,                                   `fid banded` 0.0087 0.0010)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `children`,                                    0)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `work injury`,                                 0)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `accident injury`,                             `fid banded` 0.0007 0.0003)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `unemployment`,                                `fid banded` 0.0021 0.0002)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, 0)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `disability`,                                  `fid banded` 0.0186 0.0029)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `long-term care`,                              `fid banded` 0.0014 0.0003)
       , (`A branch's column D amount` OF `senior citizens and survivors`,               `fid banded` 0.0152 0.0057)
    WHERE
        `fid banded` hi lo MEANS (min `the wage` 7703) TIMES lo PLUS (max 0 (`the wage` MINUS 7703)) TIMES hi

`fid all nine branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`
       , `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

GIVEN y       IS A NUMBER
      mo      IS A NUMBER
      wage    IS A NUMBER
      pension IS A `The senior citizen pension in the month`
      who     IS A `The insured person, for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)`
      dob     IS A DATE
      police  IS A BOOLEAN
      regs    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
`fid employee month` y mo wage pension who dob police regs MEANS
    `An employee's month under section 342(c)` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS y
        `month`                                                               IS mo
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS `fid all nine branches`
        `the column D amounts on the wage`                                    IS `fid column D amounts on a wage of` wage
        `senior citizen pension`                                              IS pension
        `the insured person`                                                  IS who
        `date of birth`                                                       IS dob
        `a police officer or a prison officer`                                IS police
        `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)` IS regs

-- An ordinary man aged 40 in February 2026, no pension, not police.
GIVEN wage IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` wage MEANS
    `fid employee month` 2026 2 wage `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1986 3 15) FALSE FALSE

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, emp IS A NUMBER, se IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An employee who is also self-employed, in a month`
`fid dual` y mo emp se MEANS
    `An employee who is also self-employed, in a month` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                                  IS y
        `month`                                                                                     IS mo
        `income from the sources in sections 2(1) and 2(8) of the Income Tax Ordinance in the month` IS se
        `income from the sources in section 2(2) of the Income Tax Ordinance in the month`          IS emp

GIVEN col IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`, wife IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)`
`fid insured` col wife MEANS
    `An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` WITH
        `column`                                                                          IS col
        `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS wife

§§ `Published figures, checked against this author's own fetch (section 1 of DECIDED-ANSWERS.md)`

-- F11 / section 2: Schedule K reads the s 2(b) average wage, 13,769, not 13,566.
#ASSERT (`the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published`)'s `the average wage as updated on 1 January` EQUALS 13769
#ASSERT (`the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published`)'s `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` EQUALS 10382
#ASSERT `the reduced collection threshold for 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute` EQUALS 7703
#ASSERT (`the full monthly minimum wage in the first month of each quarter of 2026`)'s `in January` EQUALS 6247.67
#ASSERT (`the full monthly minimum wage in the first month of each quarter of 2026`)'s `in April` EQUALS 6443.85
-- F11: with the encoding's own published figures, item 2's minimum for a quarter is on 13,769.
#ASSERT `the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 2, a self-employed person` `, for` `fid Q1` `, under` `the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published` `and` NOTHING EQUALS 10326.75

§§ `A. Who is liable, s 342(a)-(b)`

-- A1
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`fid insured` `a self-employed person` FALSE) EQUALS `the insured person, for himself`
-- A2
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`fid insured` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` FALSE) EQUALS `the insured person, for himself`
-- A3
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`fid insured` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` TRUE) EQUALS `no one: an insured woman under Chapter C only, as the wife of an insured person, is not liable`
-- A4: insured as a wife AND on another footing: the "only" flag is FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`fid insured` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` FALSE) EQUALS `the insured person, for himself`
-- A5
#ASSERT `s 342(a)-(b) — the person liable to pay the contributions for` (`fid insured` `an employee` FALSE) EQUALS `the employer, for the employee`
-- A6: with one employer, (d) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 72.80) `and the month as if paid by one employer` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 7000) EQUALS `section 342(d) does not apply: the insured person works for one employer`

§§ `B. The employee deduction, s 342(c), February 2026`

-- B1, B2, B3: at or below the bracket, the column D rows agree with their printed total (1.04).
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 7000) EQUALS 72.80
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 7702) EQUALS 80.1008
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 7703) EQUALS 80.1112
-- B4, B5, B6, B7: above the bracket. Decided on column D's printed total, 7.00.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 7704) EQUALS 80.1812
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 8000) EQUALS 100.9012
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 10000) EQUALS 240.9012
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 51910) EQUALS 3174.6012
-- B8: a wage of 60,000. The encoding does not apply the s 348(a) cap to the s 342(c) deduction; the
-- column D amounts are inputs, so the cap is the caller's. Supplied UNCAPPED, as the wage is.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 60000) EQUALS 3174.6012
-- B9: a police officer, 10,000: item 6 (unemployment) is not deducted.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 10000 `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1986 3 15) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 234.5369
-- B9' SUPPLEMENTARY: the same rule below the bracket, 7,000 x (1.04% - 0.02%).
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 7000 `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1986 3 15) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 71.40
-- B10: a man who reached 70 on 1 January 2026, no pension.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 10000 `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1956 1 1) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- B11: a man aged 69 with a senior citizen pension for the whole month.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 10000 `payable for the whole month` `a man` (YMD 1957 1 1) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- B12: a man aged 69, no pension.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 10000 `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1957 1 1) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 240.9012
-- B12' SUPPLEMENTARY: the same below the bracket.
#ASSERT `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 7000 `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1957 1 1) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 72.80
-- B14: the man of B10: the employer may reduce its own contributions by what it would have deducted.
#ASSERT `s 342(c)(2) — the amount by which the employer may reduce the contributions he is liable for, for` (`fid employee month` 2026 2 7000 `not payable for any of the month` `a man` (YMD 1956 1 1) FALSE FALSE) GREATER THAN 0

§§ `C. Several employers, s 342(d), February 2026`

-- C1: two employers at 7,000 each; coordinated on 14,000.
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 72.80, 72.80) `and the month as if paid by one employer` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 14000) EQUALS `the employee pays the difference` 375.3012
-- C2: two employers at 40,000 each (each deducted 2,340.9012); coordinated on 80,000, capped to 51,910
-- by s 348(a). The cap is applied here by the caller because the encoding does not apply it.
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 2340.9012, 2340.9012) `and the month as if paid by one employer` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 51910) EQUALS `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference` 1507.2012
-- C3: two part-time employers at 3,000 and 4,703; the total is at the bracket.
#ASSERT `s 342(d) — the outcome, for the deductions` (LIST 31.20, 48.9112) `and the month as if paid by one employer` (`fid ordinary February 2026 month on` 7703) EQUALS `neither paragraph: the actual deduction equals the coordinated contributions`

